Verify the feedback against the actual code before changing it. Address valid findings or final-verification failures with the smallest correct change. If required review feedback is incorrect or conflicts with the approved design, do not apply it blindly; record a precise justification and set `review_disputed` to true. A concern that does not reject required review feedback is not a dispute; final-verification failures are not disputes.

Add or adjust tests when the feedback exposes a coverage gap. Run only the focused tests needed to confirm the correction; the complete validation suite runs in final verification. Do not stop after reporting a patch: return a complete canonical `implementation_result` describing the entire current implementation, the disposition of all correction feedback, whether any review finding is disputed, and readiness for re-review.
